From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] comctl32: XP's common controls 6 in the XP shell session

Purpose: draw the common controls of applications in the XP shell session
as XP SP3 does, as patch 0130 does for Windows 7.
Windows behavior (xpcmp.exe, hh.exe and sh.exe on the reference XP
machine, Luna, 96 dpi): progress bars repeat the style's chunk part with
its chunk and space sizes; a status bar is 24 pixels tall whatever font it
is given, its text two pixels in; a header keeps the height the system font
gave it at creation (22 pixels) and draws the rest after its last item
with the class's part 0; a report view's label is four pixels in; list
box text two pixels in; a group box's line a pixel lower, its caption a
pixel further right and two more pixels of the line left out on both
sides; check and radio labels a pixel further left; a drop-down button one
pixel from the frame; a trackbar's channel a pixel lower; tabs: the text
a pixel further left, the selected tab's centred and the others the padding
down, unselected tabs as tall as the item and the last one a pixel
narrower.
Wine before: one band for the progress bar; the status bar and the header
sized from the font; the header's rest drawn as an item; the XP shell's
own adjustments (group box, check labels, combo button) only in the shell's
process.
Change: COMCTL32_IsXPShell() for the XP shell session, and the above
where it applies.
Evidence: every control of xpcmp.exe but the tab control is pixel-identical
to XP's (the last tab's right edge differs by a column); hh.exe and sh.exe
give XP's heights.
Scope: the XP shell session (WIN4WINE_EXTERNAL_SHELL, no WIN4WINE_SHELL).
